{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>For the seed will not be his.</b> He will not be called by his name, in the sense of \"and the firstborn whom she bears\" (Deuteronomy 25:6)." "<b>And destroyed on the ground.</b> He would destroy the seed of the *keri* and spill it outside on the ground. And I marvel at Ibn Tammim the Easterner, who explained \"and destroyed on the ground\" as that he did to her not in the manner of women, so that she would not conceive — and behold, he destroyed her ground, for upon him she sits on the ground — and this interpretation is madness, and far be it, far be it, to defile the holy seed with filth of filth." "<b>Put seed.</b> Like the infinitive [construct]."], :book :genesis, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 38, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"] ["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:47:23.151504012Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}